{"type":"stream_event","uuid":"7bae6a5d-92d8-4676-b9f8-b79502665f88","session_id":"0bc7a0e1-d40d-44b4-8483-9aafe24c8f5b","parent_tool_use_id":null,"event":{"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"input_json_delta","partial_json":"{\"archetype\":\"ui_heavy\",\"raw_user_requirement\":\"Build \\\"Midnight Table: Seven-Player Mafia\\\" - a complete social deduction game. 7 players around a circular parlor table: 1 human + 6 scripted AI personalities (Nora, Kai, Mira, Jules, Lena, Owen). Roles randomized each game: 2 Mafia, 1 Detective, 1 Doctor, 3 Villagers. Loop: Role Reveal -> Night -> Dawn -> Day Discussion -> Accusation/Hot Seat -> Vote -> Elimination/Reveal -> repeat. Town wins when both Mafia eliminated; Mafia wins when Mafia >= Town. Hidden role info preserved (human sees only own role, Mafia know partner, Detective/Doctor see private results). UI: center circular table with 7 seats showing name/color/personality/alive-dead/vote marker/claim marker/speaker ring; left panel claim ledger + vote history + death history; right panel chat + game log + input + reaction buttons; bottom phase-specific action buttons (Ask, Accuse, Defend, Claim Role, Vote, Investigate, Protect, Kill, Pass); top phase banner with timer, alive count, narrator cue. Moody detective-parlor visual style, dark room, warm table lighting, gold/red accents. Phase banner transitions (Night Falls, Dawn Breaks, Discussion Begins, Voting Begins, Victory). Scripted AI with suspicion scores per player, updates based on claims/votes/silence/accusations; Mafia AI redirects suspicion and protects partner; Town AI pressures contradictions; Detective AI may reveal/hint; Doctor AI claims cautiously. Endgame reveal screen with all roles + match summary + replay timeline. No real LLM calls - deterministic scripted AI. Scenes: Title, Role Reveal, Main Table (night/day/vote), Endgame reveal/timeline.\"}"},"message_id":"fee6e506-a947-4b0f-9359-653540aae2b0"}}
